1075 #edb/ref 17592186413429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413437 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413437 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413437 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413437 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413437 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8dd2d3fa-c650-5e37-9b97-e79bceb3c6ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413438 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9b93007b-725a-5c21-aef1-4108c8c123fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1069 "q-338917" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9\\lambda y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "827b7203-4bc8-5ef4-ada5-12343dfe7439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413439 #edb/ref 1074 "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions ${y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields $A=0.$ Thus, we have a nontrivial solution, so $\\lambda =0$ is a parameter corresponding to eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+9\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 3\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $B=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n9\\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{81}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186418250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186418251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186418252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186418253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186418254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1045 "Eigenvalues and Eigenfunctions of Homogeneous BVPs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186418250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418249 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "eea1e25f-6efb-5cef-9851-420bd75de37e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418250 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418250 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "10ec5288-96c7-54f4-a406-4dc3fa372454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418250 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418251 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418251 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "35485800-4576-505b-b01c-a3a46dd2634c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418251 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186413439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "742e6a8d-8e75-5c43-a20e-2b9e2df49b4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186391720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418253 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418253 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bab35c78-7682-5ede-95d9-455d7d62484b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418253 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186391695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418254 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418254 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "db32b2ae-bde3-5b8b-9a23-8d2e69b2eb90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921